Manual review corrections for this page's first pass.

- Item 4 and the item on the iron plate's temperature both had "and"
  joined into the surrounding math span via \text{and} with manual \,
  spacing (e.g. "$x\,\text{and}\,y$"), instead of leaving the conjunction
  as ordinary prose between two separate math spans. Rewrote as "$x$ and
  $y$".
- The level-curve item $g(x,y)=e_{}^{xy};c=\frac{1}{2},3$ carried a
  redundant empty subscript "e_{}^{xy}", a converter artifact. Removed it
  to give "e^{xy}".
- The vertical-traces section intro left the second variable of "the
  indicated values of $x$ and y" as bare prose outside math mode.
  Wrapped it as "$y$".
- The vertical trace item "$z=\cos \sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}$ $x=1$" fused two
  math spans with no separating punctuation, unlike the sibling items in
  the same list and the parallel level-curve items elsewhere in the file
  (which use a comma between the function and the fixed-variable value).
  Added the missing comma: "$z=\cos \sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}$, $x=1$".
- The electric-field item wrote "the $z\text{-axis}$" instead of the
  file's own established "$x$-axis"-style convention, and joined
  "$E=10\,\text{and}\,E=100$" the same way as the $x\,\text{and}\,y$
  defect above. Rewrote as "the $z$-axis" and "$E=10$ and $E=100$".
- The iron-plate item wrote "$xy\text{-plane.}$", trapping the sentence's
  period inside math mode alongside the plane label. Rewrote as
  "$xy$-plane." with the period outside math.
- The following item's "$P(1,2)\,is\,50^\circ \text{C}$" typeset the bare
  English word "is" inside math mode without \text, so it would render in
  math italics rather than as prose. Moved "is" outside the math span:
  "$P(1,2)$ is $50^\circ \text{C}$".
- The last item's "$T=40^\circ \text{C and}\,T=100^\circ \text{C}$" fused
  the conjunction "and" into the first \text{C} unit and joined the two
  equations into one math span. Split into "$T=40^\circ \text{C}$ and
  $T=100^\circ \text{C}$".

No mathematical content (formulas, domains, level-curve/level-surface
constants, or exercise numbering) required correction in this pass.

A later pass found twenty-two exercises across the level-curve, vertical-trace,
level-surface, and level-curve-through-a-point lists where the parameter or
point was fused to the function expression inside one math span, via either
a semicolon (e.g. "$g(x,y)=x^{2}+y^{2};c=4,c=9$") or a comma (e.g.
"$f(x,y)=3x+y^{3},x=1$", "$w(x,y,z)=x-2y+z,c=4$",
"$f(x,y)=1-4x^{2}-y^{2},P(0,1)$"), inconsistent with the two-span comma form
used by sibling items elsewhere in the file (e.g. "$z(x,y)=y^{2}-x^{2}$,
$c=1$"). Split each into two comma-joined spans to match, e.g.
"$g(x,y)=x^{2}+y^{2}$, $c=4,c=9$" and "$f(x,y)=1-4x^{2}-y^{2}$, $P(0,1)$".

